# File sections and comments

In `src/`, comment where it helps — not by file length. Prefer a few landmarks
in longer markup and notes for non-obvious intent.

## What to comment

- In Astro **markup**, use HTML comments (`<!-- ... -->`) to mark major visual
  regions when those landmarks make the template easier to scan.
- Comment non-obvious intent (dual aria text, persistence boundaries, theme
  override behavior, tenant resolution, sticky UI, etc.).
- Prefer `//` in TS/JS/CSS and Astro frontmatter / `<script>` / `<style>`.

## What not to comment

- Do not label obvious structure: `Props`, `Imports`, property names that
  already match the comment, or restating the next heading.
- Do not use `{/* ... */}` in Astro markup — that is JSX, not HTML.
- Do not comment every block. Sparse beats thorough.
- Ignore `legacy/`.

## Example

```astro
---
const { event } = Astro.props;
---

<!-- Invitation -->
<section>...</section>

<!-- Venue & map -->
<section>...</section>
```
